49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.55 Steel pipe. > 49 CFR 192.55(a)(1)
(a) New steel pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(1) It was manufactured in accordance with a listed specification;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.55 Steel pipe. > 49 CFR 192.55(b)(1)
(b) Used steel pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(1) It was manufactured in accordance with a listed specification and it meets the requirements of paragraph II-C of appendix B to this part;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.59 Plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.59(a)(1)
(a) New plastic pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(1) It is manufactured in accordance with a listed specification;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.59 Plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.59(b)(1)
(b) Used plastic pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(1) It was manufactured in accordance with a listed specification;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.59 Plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.59(b)(2)
(b) Used plastic pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(2) It is resistant to chemicals with which contact may be anticipated;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.59 Plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.59(b)(3)
(b) Used plastic pipe is qualified for use under this part if:
(3) It has been used only in gas service;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.111 Design factor (F) for steel pipe. > 49 CFR 192.111(b)(1)
(b) A design factor of 0.60 or less must be used in the design formula in § 192.105 for steel pipe in Class 1 locations that:
(1) Crosses the right-of-way of an unimproved public road, without a casing;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.111 Design factor (F) for steel pipe. > 49 CFR 192.111(b)(2)
(b) A design factor of 0.60 or less must be used in the design formula in § 192.105 for steel pipe in Class 1 locations that:
(2) Crosses without a casing, or makes a parallel encroachment on, the right-of-way of either a hard surfaced road, a highway, a public street, or a railroad;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.121 Design of plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.121(d)(i)
(d) Polyamide (PA-11) pipe requirements. (1) For PA-11 pipe produced after January 23, 2009, but before January 22, 2019, a DF of 0.40 may be used in the design formula, provided:
(i) The design pressure does not exceed 200 psig;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.121 Design of plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.121(d)(ii)
(d) Polyamide (PA-11) pipe requirements. (1) For PA-11 pipe produced after January 23, 2009, but before January 22, 2019, a DF of 0.40 may be used in the design formula, provided:
(ii) The material designation code is PA32312 or PA32316;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.121 Design of plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.121(e)(1)
(e) Polyamide (PA-12) pipe requirements. For PA-12 pipe produced after January 22, 2019, a DF of 0.40 may be used in the design formula, provided:
(1) The design pressure does not exceed 250 psig;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.121 Design of plastic pipe. > 49 CFR 192.121(e)(2)
(e) Polyamide (PA-12) pipe requirements. For PA-12 pipe produced after January 22, 2019, a DF of 0.40 may be used in the design formula, provided:
(2) The material designation code is PA42316;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.144 Qualifying metallic components. > 49 CFR 192.144(b)(1)
(b) The edition of the document under which the component was manufactured has equal or more stringent requirements for the following as an edition of that document currently or previously listed in § 192.7 or appendix B of this part:
(1) Pressure testing;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.150 Passage of internal inspection devices. > 49 CFR 192.150(b)(2)
(b) This section does not apply to: (1) Manifolds;
(2) Station piping such as at compressor stations, meter stations, or regulator stations;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.150 Passage of internal inspection devices. > 49 CFR 192.150(b)(3)
(b) This section does not apply to: (1) Manifolds;
(3) Piping associated with storage facilities, other than a continuous run of transmission line between a compressor station and storage facilities;

49 CFR Part 192 — Transportation of Natural and Other Gas by Pipeline: Minimum Federal Safety Standards — § 192.150 Passage of internal inspection devices. > 49 CFR 192.150(b)(4)
(b) This section does not apply to: (1) Manifolds;
(4) Cross-overs;

